cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CODION, please cite it as below."
title: "CODION: Cognitive Operations, Disinformation and Influence Ontology"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24103509
repository-code: "https://github.com/ESIcenter/codion-ontology"
abstract: >-
  CODION is an OWL 2 ontology for knowledge-graph representation of
  disinformation campaigns, influence operations and cognitive warfare.
  It is organised in five modules (Information and Meaning; Actors and
  Targeting; Operations; Consequences and Response; Evidence, Assessment
  and Context), uses qualified relations for attribution, targeting and
  assessment, and aligns with DISARM v1.6, FIMI, STIX 2.1, MITRE ATT&CK,
  ABCDE, ENISA, AMAS, RESIST and ETSI TR 104 159.
keywords:
  - ontology
  - OWL
  - knowledge graph
  - disinformation
  - influence operations
  - cognitive warfare
  - FIMI
  - DISARM
